# A runner fault, and the one shape in this corpus that no correct
# guest can produce: the aggregate state file says the whole job
# passed, and the log announces only one of the two members. The other
# was never built, and there is no output anywhere that says otherwise.
#
# It is here because of what the alternative would authorize. A
# promotion sums the passes over every member, so a member defaulted to
# passed on the strength of a passing job would put a port into a pull
# request on evidence that does not exist — the one way a cohort can be
# published on a build nobody ran. Errored instead: it is not a finding
# about jq, so the guest goes back, and the note says plainly that the
# guest had nothing to say about it.
# SYNTHESIZED to exercise the guard; no runner writes this: see
# README.md.
members: oniguruma jq
outcome: passed
oniguruma.state: passed
oniguruma.lint: clean
jq.state: errored
jq.detail: the guest reported no output for this subject
